## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to architect scalable per-tenant security at the API boundary without expensive per-tenant VPCs, leveraging policy-as-code and strong observability. It probes how to bind identity, authorization, and data-access controls across managed services, plus testing and rollback strategies.

## Key Concepts

- API gateway security without per-tenant VPCs
- IAP/OAuth2 for per-tenant identity
- Policy-as-code with OPA for tenant-scoped rules
- Middleware enforcement in Cloud Run and tenant tagging in logs
- CMEK key management and VPC Service Controls for egress protection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example pseudo-middleware sketch
function authorize(req, res, next) {
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const valid = opa.eval({tenant, action: req.method, path: req.path});
  if (!valid) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
```

